  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Moqi",
      "text": "*默契 — the unspoken understanding between you and your harness.*\n\n```\n ◆ moqi  tail docker logs                                              local harness\n\n▌ how do i tail the last 50 lines of a container log?"
    },
    {
      "section": "Moqi",
      "text": "A terminal app for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness),\npackaged as a `dsh` profile. A good terminal agent is one you stop having to\nexplain yourself to: Moqi keeps the conversation in the order it happened,\nputs each tool call where it was made, and gets out of the way."
    },
    {
      "section": "Highlights",
      "text": "- **Tool calls, where they happened** — each call renders inline between the\n  prose on either side of it, collapsed to one row with its own spinner and\n  status; `ctrl+o` opens the outcome underneath\n  ([docs/using-moqi.md](docs/using-moqi.md#tool-calls-where-they-happened)).\n- **Approvals that remember** — allow a command once, for this session, or\n  always (per project or everywhere); a rule like `bash(git log *)` then\n  answers matching calls without asking, and `/permissions` reviews them\n  ([docs/using-moqi.md](docs/using-moqi.md#approvals-and-permission-rules)).\n- **Memory across sessions** — the agent saves facts with `memory_save`, every\n  session sees the list, `/memory` opens it in `$EDITOR`, `# note` keeps a\n  line without sending it, and `/memory off` switches it all off\n  ([docs/using-moqi.md](docs/using-moqi.md#memory)).\n- **A branch of its own** — a new session in a git repo works on a `moqi/`\n  branch in place, or in a worktree with `/worktree`; untouched ones are\n  tidied up, and the agent is told the rules\n  ([docs/using-moqi.md](docs/using-moqi.md#branches-and-worktrees)).\n- **`shift+tab` modes** — read-only, workspace-write, or plan, on the\n  Harness's own sand"
    },
    {
      "section": "Highlights",
      "text": "Full key reference, flags, and commands: [docs/reference.md](docs/reference.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Needs Node 22+, the dsh CLI and pnpm. The same line works on Linux, macOS and\nWindows:\n\n```sh\nnpm install -g @deepseek-ai/dsh pnpm moqi-tui\nmoqi\n```\n\nThe launcher installs the profile and hands the terminal to dsh. pnpm is\nrequired because the profile is a pnpm project. Without it, `moqi install`\nstops and tells you to install it.\n\nThe dsh **desktop app** gives you no `dsh` command. Moqi needs the CLI, so run\nthe line above even if the desktop app is installed.\n\nFrom source:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/JWE24-code/moqi ~/Projects/moqi\ncd ~/Projects/moqi\nnpm install && npm run build\nnpm run install-profile\n\nUpgrading an older profile, switching Node versions, plugins in the desktop\napp, what the installer writes, and how typechecking links the Harness's own\ntypes: [docs/install.md](docs/install.md)."
    },
